{"id":4643,"date":"2026-03-12T13:14:08","date_gmt":"2026-03-12T13:14:08","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/?p=4643"},"modified":"2026-03-30T15:26:43","modified_gmt":"2026-03-30T14:26:43","slug":"when-global-climate-challenges-can-feel-overwhelming-great-ideas-for-a-resilient-and-fruitful-future-can-be-shared","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/when-global-climate-challenges-can-feel-overwhelming-great-ideas-for-a-resilient-and-fruitful-future-can-be-shared\/","title":{"rendered":"When Global Climate Challenges can Feel Overwhelming, Great Ideas for a Resilient and Fruitful Future can be Shared"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-4f7aa22\" data-block-id=\"4f7aa22\"><figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-4716 lazyload\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1923-scaled.jpg\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1437\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1923-scaled.jpg 2560w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1923-300x168.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1923-1024x575.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1923-768x431.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1923-1536x862.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1923-2048x1150.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1923-356x200.jpg 356w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1923-200x112.jpg 200w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 2560px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 2560\/1437;\" \/><\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When global climate challenges can feel overwhelming,&nbsp;great&nbsp;ideas&nbsp;for&nbsp;a more resilient future&nbsp;can be shared&nbsp;with imaginative&nbsp;nine and&nbsp;ten-year-olds.&nbsp;&nbsp;This is what the Compost Collective, winners of CCAC\u2019s 2025 Young Designer\u2019s Award,&nbsp;have just completed with Year-5 children at Lyndhurst Primary School&nbsp;in the London borough of Southwark. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The Compost Collective&nbsp;asked the children&nbsp;<em>\u201cWhat if Lyndhurst became the heart of the community in 2050? How might we design a \u2018Community Climate Hub\u2019 that helps people grow food, stay safe, share resources, and care for the planet?\u201d&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/em>Every child&nbsp;was assigned a role within their design team:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The Ecologist:&nbsp;<\/strong>Tasked with&nbsp;understanding&nbsp;the biological health of the site and the needs of local flora and fauna.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The Hydro-engineer:&nbsp;<\/strong>Focused on water management, sustainable drainage, and the impact of rainfall&nbsp;in&nbsp;urban&nbsp;areas.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The Maker-engineer:<\/strong>&nbsp;Responsible for&nbsp;identifying&nbsp;regenerative&nbsp;materials and building&nbsp;the&nbsp;team\u2019s&nbsp;design&nbsp;concepts.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The Social Designer:&nbsp;<\/strong>Dedicated to the community aspect, ensuring the designs were accessible, expressive, and served&nbsp;the people of Southwark.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-stackable-blockquote stk-block-blockquote stk-block stk-49a6a2f is-style-highlighted\" data-v=\"2\" data-block-id=\"49a6a2f\"><div class=\"has-text-align-left stk-block-blockquote__content stk-container stk-49a6a2f-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-icon stk-block-icon stk-block stk-0c35515\" data-block-id=\"0c35515\"><span class=\"stk--svg-wrapper\"><div class=\"stk--inner-svg\"><svg style=\"height:0;width:0\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"linear-gradient-0c35515\" x1=\"0\" x2=\"100%\" y1=\"0\" y2=\"0\"><stop offset=\"0%\" style=\"stop-opacity:1;stop-color:var(--linear-gradient-0-c-35515-color-1)\"><\/stop><stop offset=\"100%\" style=\"stop-opacity:1;stop-color:var(--linear-gradient-0-c-35515-color-2)\"><\/stop><\/linearGradient><\/defs><\/svg><svg xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 50 50\" aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><path d=\"M19.8 9.3C10.5 11.8 4.6 17 2.1 24.8c2.3-3.6 5.6-5.4 9.9-5.4 3.3 0 6 1.1 8.3 3.3 2.2 2.2 3.4 5 3.4 8.3 0 3.2-1.1 5.8-3.3 8-2.2 2.2-5.1 3.2-8.7 3.2-3.7 0-6.5-1.2-8.6-3.5C1 36.3 0 33.1 0 29 0 18.3 6.5 11.2 19.6 7.9l.2 1.4zm26.4 0C36.9 11.9 31 17 28.5 24.8c2.2-3.6 5.5-5.4 9.8-5.4 3.2 0 6 1.1 8.3 3.2 2.3 2.2 3.4 4.9 3.4 8.3 0 3.1-1.1 5.8-3.3 7.9-2.2 2.2-5.1 3.3-8.6 3.3-3.7 0-6.6-1.1-8.6-3.4-2.1-2.3-3.1-5.5-3.1-9.7 0-10.7 6.6-17.8 19.7-21.1l.1 1.4z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/div><\/span><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-text stk-block-text stk-block stk-081abe0\" data-block-id=\"081abe0\"><style>.stk-081abe0 .stk-block-text__text{font-size:22px !important;}@media screen and (max-width: 1023px){.stk-081abe0 .stk-block-text__text{font-size:22px !important;}}<\/style><p class=\"stk-block-text__text\"><em>\u201cThe thing I liked most was when we did the project and learned we should take care of the plants, the world, and the environment.\u201d&nbsp;<\/em>Lyndhurst year-5 pupil&nbsp;<\/p><\/div>\n<\/div><\/div><\/blockquote>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-726a57c\" data-block-id=\"726a57c\"><style>.stk-726a57c {margin-bottom:6px !important;}<\/style><figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-4707 lazyload\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1971-scaled.jpg\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1437\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1971-scaled.jpg 2560w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1971-300x168.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1971-1024x575.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1971-768x431.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1971-1536x862.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1971-2048x1150.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1971-356x200.jpg 356w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_1971-200x112.jpg 200w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 2560px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 2560\/1437;\" \/><\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>A Year-5 team\u2019s 3D model of their greenhouse that uses pipe cleaners, cardboard and lollipop sticks.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once the\u00a0child\u00a0teams\u2019\u00a0design\u00a0concepts\u00a0were\u00a0decided\u00a0and drawn,\u00a0it was time to\u00a0start\u00a0making\u00a0models\u00a0with pipe cleaners, cardboard\u00a0and\u00a0lollipop sticks\u00a0to illustrate\u00a0their\u00a0new knowledge\u00a0about how to\u00a0tackle\u00a0local climate challenges. The children displayed not only their creativity, but\u00a0demonstrated\u00a0they understood the role of\u00a0planning, social values, future proofing, and adaptation\u00a0for climate extremes.\u00a0\u00a0One\u00a0child said:\u00a0<em>\u201cI think people\u00a0should have less screen-time\u2026they should use their imagination to do stuff\u00a0like this.\u201d<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Children\u2019s Presentations<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The&nbsp;Year-5&nbsp;children&nbsp;stepped&nbsp;into the spotlight&nbsp;when they&nbsp;pitched their models and strategies to an expert&nbsp;panel.&nbsp;It was clear that they&nbsp;had&nbsp;understood the reasons for composting, rainwater harvesting and storage. They had incorporated renewable&nbsp;energy sources into their schemes and imagined crops of fruit and flowers&nbsp;in the school grounds&nbsp;irrigated by automated&nbsp;systems.&nbsp;They even spoke of the benefits of teamwork and displayed enjoyment of&nbsp;the design process:&nbsp;one said,&nbsp;<em>\u201cI loved everything and wanted more!\u201d<\/em>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-83c43b6\" data-block-id=\"83c43b6\"><style>.stk-83c43b6 {margin-bottom:0px !important;}<\/style><figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-4710 lazyload\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_7912.jpg\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1536\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_7912.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_7912-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_7912-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_7912-768x576.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_7912-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_7912-267x200.jpg 267w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/IMG_7912-167x125.jpg 167w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 2048px) 100vw, 2048px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 2048px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 2048\/1536;\" \/><\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Year-5 group of children presenting their designs and ideas to a panel.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The&nbsp;Designers\u2019&nbsp;Reveal<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Aly Tobin and Yoshimi Hata&nbsp;led the Designers\u2019&nbsp;reveal: the children were thrilled to see their concepts transformed into professional visualisations of how they imagined they would use \u201cclosed-loop systems\u201d &#8211; where food, water and energy loops are integrated to mitigate climate extremes of heat, drought and heavy rainfall in the urban landscape &#8211; and their \u201cwater flow strategies\u201d to combat flooding.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">CCAC is grateful to Compost Collective for sharing their&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;and passion with Lyndhurst&nbsp;Primary School\u2019s&nbsp;Year-5&nbsp;teachers and children. The&nbsp;outcomes are original, exciting, and represent a meaningful engagement with the climate crisis.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-9663647\" data-block-id=\"9663647\"><style>.stk-9663647 {margin-bottom:9px !important;}<\/style><figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-4714 lazyload\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-16-at-12.03.44.png\" width=\"2034\" height=\"1152\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-16-at-12.03.44.png 2034w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-16-at-12.03.44-300x170.png 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-16-at-12.03.44-1024x580.png 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-16-at-12.03.44-768x435.png 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-16-at-12.03.44-1536x870.png 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-16-at-12.03.44-353x200.png 353w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-16-at-12.03.44-200x113.png 200w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 2034px) 100vw, 2034px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 2034px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 2034\/1152;\" \/><\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Compost Collective\u2019s render of a water flow strategy system for Lyndhurst Primary School <\/em>(Credit: <em>Compost Collective)<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-c478b57\" data-block-id=\"c478b57\"><style>.stk-c478b57 .stk-img-wrapper{width:33% !important;}<\/style><figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-4468 lazyload\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/The-Portal-Trust_Beneficiary-Logo_CMYK.jpg\" width=\"33\" height=\"300\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 33px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 33\/300;\" \/><\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>This is what the Compost Collective, winners of CCAC\u2019s 2025 Young Designer\u2019s Award,\u00a0have just\u00a0completed\u00a0with\u00a0Year-5 children at Lyndhurst Primary School\u00a0in the London borough of Southwark.\u00a0<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":10,"featured_media":4720,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[12],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4643","post","type-post","status-publish","format